      "id": "q1",
      "questionType": "text",
      "question": "Explain how the S-curve of innovation adoption creates different feedback loops at different stages.",
      "maxScore": 15,
      "timeLimit": 300,
      "correctAnswer": "The S-curve of innovation adoption shows different feedback loops at different stages. In the early stage, positive feedback dominates as early adopters create visibility and reduce uncertainty for others, accelerating adoption. In the middle stage, both positive and negative feedback operate as network effects drive adoption while market saturation begins to slow growth. In the late stage, negative feedback dominates as the market becomes saturated and adoption rates decline, creating a balancing loop that stabilizes the system.",
