      "id": "q5",
      "questionType": "text",
      "question": "How do network effects create reinforcing feedback loops in innovation diffusion?",
      "maxScore": 15,
      "timeLimit": 300,
      "correctAnswer": "Network effects create reinforcing feedback loops where each additional user increases the value of the innovation for all users. This increased value attracts more users, which further increases network value, creating a virtuous cycle. The loop is reinforced by factors like reduced uncertainty, increased social proof, and improved functionality through user feedback. This positive feedback can lead to rapid adoption and market dominance, but can also create barriers to entry for competing innovations.",
